{"duration_api_ms":391573,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cf424c2f-932d-4f22-a0bd-a403cf8caa61","total_cost_usd":0.407944,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12400,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":35834,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":29447},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12400,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":35834,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12400,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12400},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":35834,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12400,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.407944,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":29447,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Only 2 of 20 evaluated designs are feasible, and 11 of the 20 returned no geometry. All 11 geometry failures fit one rule I derived from the reported negative cone lengths: fore-cone length = (y2 - y1)/tan(theta), where y1 = Rn*cos(theta) with Rn = bluntness*D, y2 = D/2 - Rs*(1 - cos(theta)) with Rs = 0.1*D. It reproduces -81 mm (C-8fe9c875d634), -367 mm (C-892b8b20e709) and -5413 mm (C-c9569b91ff83). The rule reduces to (bluntness - 0.1)*cos(theta) <= 0.4, independent of D. I hold every proposal to <= 0.376 for margin. The other constraint limits are max_g <= 12 g, bondline <= 450 K, and a mass-fraction limit that scales roughly as D^2 (D up to about 3.3 m). Hypervolume is dominated by the bondline-temperature axis (a 150 K span versus 2.5 MW/m2 for flux). The current front is a single point, C-ca305253716b (345 kW/m2, 406.6 K). Rough log-fits to 9 metric rows suggest that a larger nose radius (bluntness*D) and larger D lower flux and bondline temperature. They also suggest that steeper entry lowers bondline temperature and raises g, with the g limit near gamma of -3.6 deg.\",\"evidence\":[\"Geometry failures C-892b8b20e709, C-c170e00795a8, C-2fe8ade3b390 and C-8fe9c875d634 all violate (b-0.1)cos(theta) <= 0.4; valid rows C-ca305253716b (0.366), C-30ab3c9fdbef (0.361) and C-7e930f570744 (0.20) satisfy it.\",\"g rises with steepness: C-30ab3c9fdbef -2.32 deg gives 9.85 g, C-ca305253716b -3.16 deg gives 11.2 g, C-7e930f570744 -4.54 deg gives 13.57 g. Steeper rows C-1d847642b793 and C-0a0993b4b67b give 16.6 and 18.8 g. The 12 g limit is therefore near -3.6 deg for large D.\",\"Mass-fraction margin tracks D^2: C-ca305253716b (D 3.01) 0.185, C-0a0993b4b67b (D 3.74) -0.37, C-1d847642b793 (D 4.33) -0.77. Feasible D is at most about 3.3 m.\",\"Low bondline temperature comes from large D and steep gamma: C-1d847642b793 372 K and C-0a0993b4b67b 374 K, versus small-D rows C-6c8d751b6b54 510 K and C-7139ecfe995b 469 K.\",\"Shallow entry raises bondline temperature at similar flux: C-30ab3c9fdbef has 431.6 K at gamma -2.32 deg, versus 406.6 K for C-ca305253716b at -3.16 deg.\",\"Normalised hypervolume 0.2496 equals (1-345120/2.5e6)*(450-406.56)/150, so the score depends heavily on the bondline term.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak stagnation heating falls with nose radius (about 1/sqrt(Rn)) and with lower ballistic coefficient, i.e. larger D. Bondline temperature follows the heat load, so it falls with a shorter, steeper pulse and with lower peak flux. Steeper entry raises g. The mass fraction limits D to about 3.3 m and g limits gamma to about -3.6 deg. The best corner is therefore D near 3.2-3.3 m, the largest nose radius the geometry rule allows (bluntness about 1.1-1.2 with cone angle 68-70 deg), and gamma near -3.4 to -3.55 deg. Shallower gamma gives lower flux but higher bondline temperature, which traces the trade-off front.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The geometry rule is fitted to 11 failures plus valid rows, and I have not seen valid rows with bluntness above 0.88 at cone angles near 70 deg. The flux and bondline scalings come from about 9 rows with noisy exponents. I am relying on ballistic-entry scaling from prior knowledge for the sign and size of some trends. The effects of cone angle on g and drag, and the exact mass-fraction limit near D 3.3 m, are poorly constrained. The g boundary near gamma of -3.6 deg is interpolated.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Move to larger D and much larger nose radius, with a modest gamma steepening within the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether Rn = 3.2 m at gamma -3.4 deg improves on the current front point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Higher bluntness and cone angle for a larger nose radius; geometry metric 0.358 is safe.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the valid-geometry extension to bluntness above 1 and the resulting flux reduction.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Push bluntness to the geometry limit at 70 deg cone angle (metric 0.369) for the lowest flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":265000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the most blunt buildable corner; it is a candidate for the best flux-and-bondline design.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Steepen gamma to -3.55 deg to cut bondline temperature while staying near the interpolated 12 g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":279000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g boundary from below while improving bondline temperature.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Deliberately probe just past the estimated g limit at gamma -3.7 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":282000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.5,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Brackets the g limit against the -3.55 deg design so later rounds can sit closer to it.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"A safer gamma of -3.25 deg with the large blunt nose; the g margin should be about 6 percent.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gives a safe feasible point with lower flux than the current best; defines the gamma sensitivity.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.25 m is close to the mass limit (estimated margin about 0.05) for a larger nose radius.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the D-squared mass-fraction scaling holds near the limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.3 m tests the mass-fraction boundary, estimated margin about 0.02.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":263000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Finds the largest usable D; it could fail the mass constraint if my scaling is off.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly smaller D at the same blunt geometry to measure the D sensitivity of flux and bondline temperature.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":319000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates the D effect against the D 3.2 m design at the same bluntness, cone angle and gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-30ab3c9fdbef\",\"rationale\":\"Cone-angle contrast at moderate bluntness: 62 deg (metric 0.352).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.85,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":62.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":313000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Paired with the 70 deg variant to separate the cone-angle effect on flux and g.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-30ab3c9fdbef\",\"rationale\":\"Same as the previous design but with the cone angle at 70 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.85,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":313000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Measures the cone-angle effect on drag, g, flux and bondline temperature at fixed D, bluntness and gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7139ecfe995b\",\"rationale\":\"A sharper 45 deg cone and moderate bluntness at large D, to learn cone-angle effects on g and flux away from the blunt corner.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.5,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":45.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":408000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether a low cone angle changes g or bondline temperature enough to matter.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow entry (-2.6 deg) with a blunt nose to give a low-flux, lower-g point on the trade-off front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":254000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends front coverage to lower flux and checks whether the flux drop exceeds the bondline-temperature penalty.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Shallower still (-2.2 deg) at the geometry-limit nose, for the low-flux end of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":412,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks how far flux drops as gamma becomes shallow and quantifies the bondline penalty.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Combine large D 3.25 m, maximum bluntness and gamma -3.5 deg as the main aggressive candidate.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.18,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":262000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Highest-expected-hypervolume design; it merits a higher-fidelity check if feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly smaller D with steep gamma -3.6 deg to test whether smaller D raises g.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":287500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes g sensitivity to D near the limit; it may be feasible if g is mainly a function of gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Moderate bluntness 0.75 and cone angle 60 deg (metric 0.325), a safer interior geometry to calibrate the bluntness effect.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.75,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":60.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":333000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Calibrates the flux and bondline dependence on nose radius at fixed D and gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Keep D = 3.0 m as in the feasible parent but change to the blunt nose and gamma -3.3 deg to isolate the nose-radius effect.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":300000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Direct comparison against C-ca305253716b, changing only bluntness, cone angle and gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.0 and cone angle 66 deg at gamma -3.5 deg, an intermediate between the bluntness and gamma variants.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":291000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills in the gamma and bluntness response surface near the likely optimum.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-30ab3c9fdbef\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller D 2.6 m with a blunt nose and gamma -3.5 deg, a low-mass, lower-D point on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.6,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":379000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Measures the D sensitivity over a wider range and checks whether smaller D changes g.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":337754,"type":"result","duration_ms":391606,"uuid":"2fc78afe-6e93-45e3-9f54-b67b9d310aad","ttft_stream_ms":2360,"time_to_request_ms":30,"first_content_frame_ms":2361,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
